{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"=== EPIC REMEDIATION (post-handoff, operator-requested) ===\n\nAudited epic 1386's acceptance criteria against the real state of src/rebar/ and remediated it so it can actually be completed. Intent preserved throughout: collapse Success Criteria into a single Acceptance Criteria vocabulary. Only false-positive carve-outs were made explicit, exactly as O-RAN-SC and the vendor bundle already were.\n\nEPIC EDITS (4 ACs + Scope):\n- Scope/OUT OF SCOPE: the dod_uncertifiable exclusion said 'in the verifier prompts', which missed the IDENTICAL wording in llm/review_kernel/verify_models.py:231 - now names all three sites. Added plan_review_T2.md's 'stated success criteria for a trial' (generic English about an experiment succeeding; 2aa6's AC6 requires it to survive).\n- AC1: was 'No live source file under src/rebar/ matches ...' - contradicted the epic's OWN Scope and 2aa6's AC6, so unsatisfiable. Now: grep returns matches ONLY at the four excluded sites + vendor bundle, with the exact verifying command.\n- AC4: was 'The 108 store tickets ...' - now count-agnostic (recomputed at run time) and records the actual: 106 migrated, 0 SC headings remain, 8 prose mentions correctly untouched. Also clarifies a backticked prose mention is not a heading.\n- AC5: was 'contains no SC vocabulary' - impossible, since the guide is GENERATED from the registry and embeds T2's excluded prompt verbatim. Now pins EXACTLY ONE match, which is STRICTER (also proves the phrase survived rather than being dropped).\n\nGAP FOUND BY THE AUDIT: src/rebar/llm/completion.py:288 ('its success criteria are met across children') is genuine heading-sense vocabulary owned by NO child story - 35bc did detectors, 2aa6 the reviewer prompts, 93d0 the eval specs, 44c7 the guides/docs, and none reaches completion.py. Epic AC1 could never have passed. Assigned to 5f4d (scope + file_impact).\n\nCHILD UPDATES:\n- 5f4d: gained completion.py:288 as a sweep target; guard allowlist gained the four permanent carve-outs (T2 + the three dod_uncertifiable sites), the 35bc contract test tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_criteria_heading_collapse.py, and the GENERATED criteria guide.\n- 93d0 + 44c7: commented with the carve-outs they must NOT 'fix', plus the epic AC5 change.\n\nPROOF OF SATISFIABILITY: grep -rniE 'success[ _-]criteri(a|on)' src/rebar/ minus the exclusions now returns ONLY _guides/writing-a-passing-plan.md (44c7), eval_specs/*.eval.yaml + evals/eval_solver.py (93d0), and llm/completion.py (5f4d). Every remaining match is owned by a remaining story. The generated guide already sits at exactly one match, satisfying amended AC5 today.\n\nEPIC ATTESTATION: stale-code (4 dependency files drifted when 35bc landed: gates.py, assemble.py, eval_solver.py, det_floor.py). A fresh review-plan was launched to refresh it; result recorded below/next."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785018831522037001,"uuid":"f35d61f4-d016-4715-8da7-170e64b54b3a"}